# One attack key of B's creature wounds the shared ripper, seen on A's machine, in four tries.
# The root trap holds the ripper still on both machines, so the attacks are tested, not the aim.
# Parameters: key (PrimaryAttack, SecondaryAttack or Dodge), at (distance to strike from), gap (seconds between tries), ripper.

A effect add StatusEffect_RootTrap_Root $ripper
B effect add StatusEffect_RootTrap_Root $ripper
A health $ripper mark
B tpnear $ripper $at 0
B look $ripper
B expect press $key 0.2 !contains "Stunned" timeout=10
sleep $gap
B tpnear $ripper $at 0
B look $ripper
B expect press $key 0.2 !contains "Stunned" timeout=10
sleep $gap
B tpnear $ripper $at 0
B look $ripper
B expect press $key 0.2 !contains "Stunned" timeout=10
sleep $gap
B tpnear $ripper $at 0
B look $ripper
B expect press $key 0.2 !contains "Stunned" timeout=10
A expect health $ripper lost >= 1 timeout=8
